{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15892-shows-to-watch-for-inspiration","id":15892,"title":"Shows to watch for Inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-21T22:26:25-08:00","id":15892,"title":"Shows to watch for Inspiration","content":"I know we have a few specific threads, but a more general one might be of service. What television series' might you suggest for inspiration for a Demon chronicle?<br /> <br /> I just started watching <i>Fringe</i> a few weeks back, and it is a fantastic fit. A small handful of FBI agents are dealing with strange cases that all fit into a grand scheme known only as &quot;the Pattern.&quot; The corporation known as Massive Dynamics always seems to be involved. There's strange, inhuman observers, and at least one alternate timeline at play. Fascinating stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T00:20:15-08:00","id":15934,"title":"","content":"The Twilight Zone has a TON of inspiration for Stigmatics and ideas for Pacts.<br /> <br /> A couple of other old shows would be The Prisoner and probably Twin Peaks (though I haven't seen either yet).<br /> <br /> And of course there's Burn Notice, one of the best shows about being a spy ever because <i>it teaches you how to espionage.</i> Espionate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":".  moar shows 11-22-2013, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T00:56:51-08:00","id":15955,"title":"","content":"even though no tv series by itself. angel sanctuary has a few good ideas (anime ova. and manga). a specific angel there can make humans and angels his servants by turning them into anorganic beings, a computer prigram that uses the life force of humans to resurrect a powerful angel, ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T02:02:36-08:00","id":15983,"title":"","content":"Person of Interest, obviously.<br /> <br /> The Melancholy of Haruhi Suzumiya includes a couple of characters who are pretty much G-M Angels. They're meat puppets sent by a god-like alien being known as the Data Integration Thought Entity, which can manipulate reality via changing the data that composes it, to observe a human with unusual powers. However, the two agents disagree in how best to observe the subject, which leads to the following fight:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZvmbKkmqbSM\" data-code=\"ZvmbKkmqbSM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZvmbKkmqbSM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T02:20:18-08:00","id":16000,"title":"","content":"Along the lines of Fringe, I think Lost makes a great inspiration. It's the God-Machine's schemes seen through the eyes of humans subtly manipulated to fulfill a very obscure fate. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There are Infrastructures on that damn island. Strings of numbers that happen to be very important to the universe, and can be used as &quot;cheat codes&quot; with awful consequences. Cults. Time travel. A Saboteur with the strange ability to take anyone as a Cover, as long as they're already dead. An Angel doing a kinda shoddy job, until he gets replaced by... a duo of Stigmatics promoted to Angels? Something like that.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T09:03:22-08:00","id":16126,"title":"","content":"Leverage, Chuck, Burn Notice, Sarah Conner Chronicles, Fringe, the X-Files, Alias, Continuum. All good, directly-inspiring fodder for Demon: the Descent. Dollhouse, too, but I found that show way too infuriating to consider fodder for anything but <i>enraged constipation. </i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T15:42:24-08:00","id":20828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15892-shows-to-watch-for-inspiration?p=15983#post15983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Melancholy of Haruhi Suzumiya includes a couple of characters who are pretty much G-M Angels. They're meat puppets sent by a god-like alien being known as the Data Integration Thought Entity, which can manipulate reality via changing the data that composes it, to observe a human with unusual powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to cite Nagato, Asakura and the other humanoid interfaces of the Data Overmind (as Yen Press translates <i>Joh\u014d T\u014dg\u014d Shinen-Tai</i>) as examples of angels (in large part because I'm currently reading the final light novel, <i>The Surprise of Haruhi Suzumiya</i>) if nobody else had. Also, because it's returned to [adult swim], I've seen, and must therefore point to, Gainax's insanely wacky <i>FLCL</i> (pronounced &quot;Fooly Cooly&quot; and recorded under that name by my household's Dish Network DVR). The Medical Mechanica building, headquarters of the puzzling conspiracy that drives the plot, is obviously Infrastructure, and protagonist Naota &quot;Takkun&quot; Nandaba is one of the stranger stigmatics imaginable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T15:52:01-08:00","id":20833,"title":"","content":"The News.<br /> <br /> Or at least any good serious news channel, particularly ones that focus on politics. If you can get access to channels that broadcast inquiries or legal proceedings those could be great too.<br /> <br /> They're probably the closest you'll get to seeing the real evidence that people collect and use to try and determine what happened.<br /> <br /> Tabloids would also probably be pretty good, see the dirty gossip about whatever celebrity marriage break ups, the mud slinging and so on, the evidence from email trails and the like.<br /> <br /> You want your PCs to be finding snippets and clues? Why wait for fiction when the real world political scene is essentially nothing more than a Soap Opera with serious outcomes?<br /> <br /> Trawl Wikipedia for interesting court cases, historical ones are likely to have a fairly decent bit of the evidence presented in the article.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> For Infrastructure/Arcane Matrices I'd...well...anything will do. Do you have a mechanical watch? Maybe the second hand gets stuck when it runs past 54 seconds erratically? I wonder why that could be? Is it sticking when something unbalances the mechanism inside? Perhaps it's running on an entirely different unit of time and each time it sticks is one unit of that alternate time passing? Who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T12:03:30-08:00","id":22492,"title":"","content":"I realized that Digital Devil Saga (okay, a video game, not a TV show) is a good inspiration as well.<br /> This game of the Shin Megami Tensei series (all of which featuring a lot of judeo-christian images, culminating generally with the possibility to beat up/team up with Satan and beat up God for being an asshole, oh, and He's aligned with Law/Order and his Angel minions are pricks) starts with Demon protagonists. Well, they appear (mostly) human, but are usually meant to fight in their very weird demonic form; the 2nd game also forces them into a hybrid form, where they manifest only a couple demonic features, upon certain circumstances. They believe there is another world out there they can reach, one that is much better to live in.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In the 2nd game, they end up in the real world; you see, the events of the 1st game took place in a simulation, and the PCs were all AIs. Thing is, it turns out there's not a whole lot of difference between their virtual world and ours, since both are made out of data. The real world is hardly better than the one they started in, and God is to blame (okay, there are other culprits, but God doesn't help at all), so they need to kick His ass. Conclusion of the story: they die in the process, but are reincarnated/find enlightenment, and have managed to make reality a much better place to live in, without God's nefarious influence.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> The concept of reality as a sort of computer simulation is big here.<br /> This game, unlike the others, focuses on Hindu and Buddhist imagery and ignores a lot of the other religions, but it resonates well with D:tD, I think.<br /> In fact, if it's a Shin Megami Tensei game, it's probably a good inspiration for nWoD. They're all dark to a degree, and while the supernatural hardly makes anything better, you bet mundane humans are to blame for a bunch of the shit that's going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":519,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","user":"ChairKicker","date":". 12-03-2013, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}